Z||000000||DaveL||06-30-2000||03:55 PM||||I have an 87 Se 2.5 DIS, THM 125, with about 80,000 miles on it. The tranny occasionally acts up in an odd sort of way. Normally it shifts perfectly, ending up in third gear then overdrive around 30 mph, under no real load. Does the same under full throttle acceleration. But then, every now and then it won't shift into second from first until I hit around 3200 rpm. If I let off the gas before it shifts into second, the engine idles way down with no motor braking effect. To continue to accelerate, when I push the pedal, the motor revs until it catches up to the speed the vehicle is traveling, then accelerates until the shift. Sometimes, it wont shift from second into third until I hit about 3000 rpm. While its in second, if I let off the gas the car slows with the engine. In other words, it stays engaged. Happens at unpredictable intervals, then stops acting up abruptly. I have changed the fluid and filter, and had the tranyy flush treatment, no real change. Rebuild time?<BR>Also, I have aquired a rear cradle with the THM125, axles, and rotors and drums from an unidentified Fiero. Are there any numbers to identify the tranny with? Want to know if its worth having rebuilt out of the car so I can do a quick change if needed.||||reg||5
Z||000001||shain||07-01-2000||07:44 AM||||your tranny is cooked!! rebuild or get a new one. had this happen (not as bad) on an 85 buick regal somerset w/2.5. ||||reg||9
